# Add GitHub Integration & Update Badge Logic

The user pointed out that the "Git Starter" badge logic requires the student's GitHub to be connected, but there's currently no way for the student to link their GitHub profile.

## Proposed Changes

We will add a feature allowing students to link their GitHub username directly from their Profile page, and update the badge logic to reward them for this action.

### 1. Database Schema
#### [MODIFY] `supabase/migrations/001_create_tables.sql`
- Add `github_username TEXT` column to the `profiles` table.
- Since we can't easily re-run the entire migration if the database is already seeded/active without wiping it, I will execute an `ALTER TABLE` SQL command to safely add this column to the existing database in the background, and also update the migration file for future deployments.

### 2. Server Actions
#### [MODIFY] `src/features/auth/actions/auth.ts`
- Add a new server action `updateGithubUsername(userId: string, username: string)` to safely update the profile.

#### [MODIFY] `src/features/gamification/actions/gamification.ts`
- Update the `github_count` condition check. Currently it checks for "approved submissions with a github link". We will modify it so that if a user simply connects their GitHub profile (i.e. `profile.github_username` is not null), they are immediately eligible for the "Git Starter" badge.

### 3. Profile UI
#### [NEW] `src/app/(dashboard)/profile/components/GithubConnect.tsx`
- Create a new Client Component for the sidebar of the Profile page.
- It will feature a sleek UI allowing users to input and save their GitHub username.
- If already connected, it will show their username and a link to their GitHub profile (`https://github.com/username`), along with an "Edit" option.

#### [MODIFY] `src/app/(dashboard)/profile/page.tsx`
- Import and render the new `GithubConnect` component inside the `.profile-col-side` column, right above or below the "Recent Activity" section.

